<title>FRANCE: Aerospatiale 96 net profit 812 mln.</title>
<headline>Aerospatiale 96 net profit 812 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		    812  vs   loss    981</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)			 50.9  vs	    49.2</p>
<p>    Order book (billions)		    129.9  vs	   101.5</p>
<p>    Operating profit			     736  vs   profit  639</p>
<p>    New orders (billions)		     63.3  vs	    39.3</p>
<p>    Investments (billions)		     1.8  vs	     1.5</p>
<p>    Net debt (billion)			   2.9 no comparison</p>
<p>    Equity capital (billions)		  4.9 no comparison</p>
<p>NOTE - Societe Nationale Industrielle Aerospatiale gave its results in a statement. &quot;The results for the 1997 year should...see a very significant turn in the group's profitability, allowing a doubling of profits,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The start of 1997 had been marked by commercial success and restructuring efforts were being confirmed. The dollar has risen 10 percent compared to its average market rate in 1996.</p>
<p>By the end of 1997, it will have delivered more than 190 planes to Airbus Industrie, compared to 126 last year, bringing turnover to around 60 billion francs, representing a rise of 18 percent. The effects of cost cutting measures begun in 1995 will have their full effect during this year.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 jmb/pnt</p>
